From: flip
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: weeknd: report the power key as KEY_POWER

The red end/power key was KEY_HANGUP_PHONE, which systemd-logind ignores,
so the key did nothing under Debian. Report KEY_POWER; logind is set to
power off on a long press and ignore short presses (left to call apps).

diff --git i/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qm215-nokia-weeknd.dts w/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qm215-nokia-weeknd.dts
--- i/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qm215-nokia-weeknd.dts
+++ w/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/qm215-nokia-weeknd.dts
@@ -377,7 +377,12 @@
 };
 
 &pm8916_pwrkey {
-	linux,code = <KEY_HANGUP_PHONE>;
+	/*
+	 * The red end/power key. KEY_POWER lets systemd-logind act on a
+	 * long press (poweroff); a short press is left to the phone apps
+	 * (end call), with HandlePowerKey=ignore.
+	 */
+	linux,code = <KEY_POWER>;
 };
 
 &pm8916_resin {
